     3	1. Observation 1 — degenerate exposure strata
     4	
     5	Evidence: all 103 nominal targets have `K0 = K1 = 1.0` median exposures/night; K2 is 1.0 for 71 targets and 2.0 for 32. Thus the planned exposure stratification did not occur, as already noted in the [pilot README](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/results/2026-08-30_d2_pilot/README.md:36).
     6	
     7	The frozen estimator remains mathematically well-defined:
     8	
     9	\[
    10	\hat p=\frac1{103}\sum_t\frac13\sum_k y_{tk}.
    11	\]
    12	
    13	With complete results it is the exact mean over the fixed 309-shard schedule. But “unbiased” needs qualification:
    14	
    15	- It is exact for that finite, deterministic three-window design.
    16	- It is not design-unbiased for the 928-window population because the windows were not randomly sampled.
    17	- It is not an exposure-stratified estimate, and relabelling K as replicates cannot make the deterministically selected, source-ID-tie-broken windows exchangeable.
    18	- The target bootstrap remains appropriate only for the prespecified target-superpopulation interpretation conditional on those windows, as stated in the [metrics specification](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:152).
    19	
    20	I recommend re-stratification, not merely relabelling. A mechanism-aligned covariate is
    21	
    22	\[
    23	n_{\mathrm{eff},zg}=\sum_{\text{night}}n_{\text{night}}\mathbf1(n_{\text{night}}\ge2),
    24	\]
    25	
    26	the number of zg exposures on nights that are not annihilated by single-exposure nightly subtraction. Across the 928 windows its 10/50/90 percentiles are 12/104/724. Selecting target-specific 10/50/90 positions by this variable gives strict K0<K1<K2 separation for 103/103 targets, with selected medians 12/107/691. Baseline is non-degenerate but much more compressed and is less directly tied to the stated failure mechanism.
    27	
    28	Recommendation: regenerate gen1 with low/median/high effective-zg-support strata. Report the surface against raw \(n_{\mathrm{eff},zg}\), not “exposures per night,” with both `n_targets` and `n_windows`, target-equal estimates, and target-cluster intervals. If regeneration were declined, K must be called `replicate_id`, and the existing exposure surface should be reported only as observed 1-versus-2 support with no exposure-gradient claim.
    29	
    30	2. Observation 2 — P4 construct validity and controls
    31	
    32	Evidence: nominal B produced 16/30 detections but only 7/30 strict dominant-frequency recoveries [in the P4 table](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/results/2026-08-30_d2_pilot/metrics/d2_cluster_completeness.csv:54). By template status:
    33	
    34	- Published confirmed: detection 11/13, strict recovery 2/13.
    35	- Published not-detected: detection 4/15, strict recovery 4/15.
    36	- Published candidate: detection 1/2, strict recovery 1/2.
    37	
    38	Moreover, 53/119 unique nominal windows are published confirmed, and the ten pilot controls reproduced published trigger status 10/10. These results support the [README’s construct-validity concern](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/results/2026-08-30_d2_pilot/README.md:43): detection-only mostly measures whether the combined light curve triggers, not whether the injected DAV signal was recovered.
    39	
    40	Recommendation:
    41	
    42	- Make `confirmed AND best_candidate_matches_dominant == direct` the primary/headline P4 estimand.
    43	- Retain detection-only as a key secondary endpoint named “post-injection trigger rate,” not “injection-recovery completeness.”
    44	- Do not condition the primary analysis on the control being non-triggering; that changes the denominator to a selected, status-dependent subset.
    45	- Do not subtract the aggregate 119-control native-trigger rate from P4.
    46	- The emitted census/L-S discordance is method complementarity within injected B and does not address uninjected controls.
    47	
    48	Instead, score every paired control against the truth of each B shard to which it is paired. For both detection \(D\) and strict recovery \(R\), report the B/control 2×2, B-only yield, control-only yield, union, and paired mean difference. In particular,
    49	
    50	\[
    51	R^C_{tk}=1\{\text{control confirmed and its best frequency directly matches target }t\text{’s dominant injected mode}\}.
