generalization/reviews/G4/PROMPT_stats.md:1:G4 — pilot metrics sanity (STATISTICS lens). Read generalization/results/2026-08-30_d2_pilot/README.md and its metrics/ (per_star.csv, d2_cluster_completeness.csv, d2_scenario_contrasts.csv, trigger_rates.csv, sensitivity.csv, fp_frequency_distribution.csv, manifest.json), run/shard_manifest_gen1.csv and run/generation_manifest_gen1.json, plus the frozen estimands in generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md (P4 detection completeness — nominal arm B; P5 FPR_Gaussian; frequency-recovery completeness; paired controls; scenario contrasts) and the D2 design in generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md. The pilot is non-confirmatory (144 shards, 10 targets). Questions, each with evidence and a recommendation: (1) OBSERVATION 1 — the exposures-per-night strata are degenerate (pool quantiles 1.0/1.0/2.0; K0 == K1 for 103/103 targets): does the frozen P4 estimator (equal-weight mean over targets of the per-target mean over K strata) remain well-defined and unbiased as a "three matched replicate windows" design, and how should the completeness surface's exposure axis be reported? Should the strata be re-labelled (replicates), or re-stratified by a non-degenerate window covariate (e.g. number of zg exposures or baseline) via an Amendment 4 that regenerates gen1 (cheap; no confirmatory run exists)? (2) OBSERVATION 2 — 342/928 pool windows are published variables; detection-only P4 on confirmed windows confirms 11/13 but recovers the injected frequency 2/13; nominal-B recovery on not_detected windows is 4/15, all direct. Is P4 (detection-only) still the right primary D2 estimand, or should the prespecified frequency-recovery endpoint (confirmed AND dominant mode direct) become the headline with detection-only reported alongside, and how exactly should the paired uninjected controls enter (e.g. per-window native-trigger adjustment, conditioning on control status, or the paired census/L-S discordance already emitted)? Any change is an Amendment 4 to be prespecified BEFORE the full run. (3) P5: with 1,000 nulls, is the CP-at-observed-x acceptance (U95 ≤ 0.005) still the right confirmatory design given the pilot's 0/30? (4) Any statistical anomaly in the outputs (e.g. bootstrap intervals, contrasts at n=3, chance-match calibration) that would compromise the full run. Output: numbered answers, an explicit recommended Amendment 4 text (or "no amendment"), then "## Verdict: PROCEED-AS-IS | PROCEED-WITH-AMENDMENT-4 | HOLD". Do not edit files.
