     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""D2 truth model: analytic DAV signals for injection into real ZTF windows.
     3	
     4	Why a truth model and not interpolation: DAV periods reach below twice the
     5	TESS 120-s cadence (super-Nyquist) and below the first sinc null; interpolated
     6	TESS photometry is undefined there. The published mode solution (period,
     7	amplitude) IS the measurement — we evaluate it analytically at the template's
     8	real BJD_TDB epochs.
     9	
    10	Amplitude chain (GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md, D2):
    11	  A_ppt (published, TESS-integrated, PDCSAP = already crowding-corrected —
    12	         Romero+2022 and Romero+2025 both state their amplitudes are
    13	         dilution-corrected)
    14	    -> fractional flux (x 1e-3)
    15	    -> crowding sensitivity (G3 numerics finding 4): the prespecified variant
    16	       is the SAP-EQUIVALENT RE-DILUTION, A_variant = A_PDCSAP x CROWDSAP
    17	       (multiplication; dividing PDCSAP by CROWDSAP again would inflate the
    18	       injected amplitude ~5x at the median CROWDSAP of 0.19). OFF by default
    19	       (crowdsap=None); scheduled only for SPOC-verified stars.
    20	    -> de-integrate the TESS exposure: divide by sinc(pi f T_cad);
    21	       REJECT modes with |sinc| < 0.3 (do not amplify model error > 3.3x).
    22	       At T=120 s this cutoff is P < ~160.0 s; at 20 s, P < ~26.7 s.
    23	    -> magnitudes (x 1.0857)
    24	    -> bandpass ladder: A_g = R_g * A_TESS_intrinsic, A_r = R_rg * A_g with
    25	       R_g in {1.4, 1.7, 2.1}, R_rg in {0.70, 0.80, 0.90}; blackbody T-derivative
    26	       ratios at Teff ~ 11,500 K give (1.43, 0.80) — the ladder's low rung;
    27	       empirical DAV multi-band ratios (limb darkening + nonadiabatic boost in
    28	       the blue) motivate the upper rungs. Nominal (1.7, 0.80). Headline
    29	       numbers are quoted as the band across the ladder.
    30	    -> re-integrate the ZTF 30-s exposure: multiply by sinc(pi f 30s).
    31	
    32	Phase protocol (frozen): each mode of the COMPLETE published mode list gets
    33	ONE independent phase, drawn in published-table order BEFORE sinc rejection
    34	and before any dropout, so a mode's phase is a function of (TIC, phase_draw,
    35	table position) only. The base assignment (phase_draw=0) seeds PCG64(TIC) and
    36	is shared across bands and across every bandpass/crowding/amplitude-scale/
    37	dropout variant (variant-stable). The two phase-draw sensitivity variants
    38	d in {1, 2} seed PCG64(TIC*10 + d) — the ONLY thing that changes between phase
    39	draws is the phase vector. A shared t_ref keeps the two-band evidence rule
    40	meaningful.
    41	
    42	Dominant-mode dropout (G3 numerics finding 3): the dropped mode is the
    43	largest-amplitude RETAINED (post-sinc) mode; every surviving mode keeps the
    44	phase it has in the nominal model; dropout is defined only when >= 2 modes are
    45	retained (the builder checks `retained_modes` first).
    46	
    47	This module also owns the D2 manifest CONTRACT (column schema + scenario
    48	codes) so the shard builder and the metrics program cannot drift apart.
    49	"""
