     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Synthesize D2 exposure shards: DAV truth signals in real ZTF windows.
     3	
     4	Template pool: ALL 928 stars of the published 2026-08-01 catalog — NOT the
     5	510 not-detected subset (G1 referee finding 1: conditioning templates on the
     6	pipeline's own non-detection is a circularity path). Native variability is
     7	handled by frequency-matched scoring plus paired controls. Every shard
     8	preserves the template's real epochs (bjd_tdb), real cadence structure and
     9	real magerr; arms differ in what carries the noise:
    10	
    11	  arm B (92…)  signal added to the REAL ZTF magnitudes — the headline arm
    12	               ("TESS-truth signals injected into real ZTF photometry").
    13	  ctrl (95…)   paired uninjected copy of every unique arm-B template window —
    14	               identifies windows that trigger natively (real variables in
    15	               the pool), so injected-recovery is scored against its own
    16	               window's baseline behavior.
    17	  arm A (93…)  signal added to a synthetic Gaussian floor (median mag +
    18	               N(0, magerr_i)) — diagnostic; separates window effects from
    19	               real-noise effects.
    20	  nulls (94…)  arm-A construction with amplitude_scale = 0 — 1,000 shards
    21	               cycling the 928 windows with distinct noise seeds (windows
    22	               repeat, noise does not). This measures the GAUSSIAN-NULL
    23	               false-alarm rate, not a real-sky FPR (G1 stats finding 11).
    24	
    25	Templates are the ATTESTED per-star exposure shards the frozen pipeline
    26	consumed (`--exposure-stars`), not a re-derivation: every non-modified column
    27	is copied as its ORIGINAL TEXT TOKEN, the model is evaluated on the epochs as
    28	the frozen loader parses them, and each written shard is re-loaded through the
    29	frozen loader and checked bitwise (epochs) before it counts (G3 methods
    30	finding 7 — a 17-significant-digit BJD can re-parse one ulp off on the
    31	production machine, so tokens, not floats, are what is preserved).
    32	
    33	Template matching per target: |median zg mag − target G| <= 0.25 (widened to
    34	0.5, then nearest-9, when the pool is thin — flagged in the manifest);
    35	K=3 at the 10/50/90th percentiles of median-exposures-per-night, because 75%
    36	of zg nights are single-exposure and per-night median subtraction is the
    37	pre-registered dominant penalty (plan risk 3). Ties: stable sort on
    38	(|Δmag|, source_id), then (exp_per_night, source_id) — a total order.
    39	
    40	Run matrix (plan): nominal (1.7, 0.80) on K=3 for arms A+B; every other
    41	scenario on the median template (K=1) only; 1,000 nulls; one control per
    42	unique arm-B window. Targets with ZERO retained modes at nominal cannot be
    43	positives and are excluded from the matrix (recorded in
    44	excluded_targets.csv); dropout is scheduled only for targets with >= 2
    45	retained modes.
    46	
    47	Scenario identity is an explicit immutable code (d2_truth_model.scenario_code)
    48	carried on every manifest row; the manifest schema is fixed
    49	(d2_truth_model.MANIFEST_COLUMNS) and every row of every arm is fully typed.
    50	
    51	Generation discipline (G3 methods finding 3): shards are built into a staging
    52	directory carrying an IN_PROGRESS sentinel, validated (index == manifest ==
    53	disk, bijections, SHAs), described by generation_manifest.json (a generation
    54	id derived from every input SHA + code SHAs + arguments), and only then
    55	published atomically by renaming the staging directory into place. There is
    56	no resume: a generation is all-or-nothing.
    57	
    58	Truth preservation (G2 methods finding 4): every shard's actually-injected
    59	modes (post sinc rejection, with signed factors and phases) go to
    60	injected_modes.csv and the rejected ones to rejected_modes.csv; the metrics
    61	scorer consumes injected_modes.csv, never the original mode table.
    62	
    63	A stratified pilot_shard_index.txt (~150 shards spanning every arm and
    64	scenario, window strata and target amplitudes) is always emitted for the
    65	timing pilot (run it with --stars-file); pilot outputs are never
    66	confirmatory (G3 methods finding 8).
