     1	# Generalization campaign: three-dataset response assessment of the frozen pipeline
     2	
     3	Branch `generalization/campaign-1` · frozen baseline tag `frozen-2026-08-01` ·
     4	deadline AAS 249 regular abstract Wed 2026-09-30.
     5	
     6	## Claim under test
     7	
     8	The 2026-08-01 ZTF white-dwarf run showed the variance census and the blind
     9	Lomb-Scargle search have complementary selection functions — but on 19
    10	truth-labeled stars, with a known mechanism, and injections conditioned on two
    11	light curves. Red-team verdict: NO-GO as a discovery claim. The flip condition:
    12	run the *frozen* pipeline on externally labeled samples large enough to
    13	measure class-specific response rates with uncertainty.
    14	
    15	G1 review (sol ×3, 2026-08-28) sharpened what this campaign can honestly
    16	claim — THREE SEPARATE response assessments, never pooled into one
    17	"selection function":
    18	- D1: the anchor (19 labeled WDs + 928-star catalog, published);
    19	- D2: conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the frozen search stage
    20	  (TESS-truth signals in real ZTF windows) — labeled as such, NOT real-sky
    21	  completeness and NOT an independently labeled sample;
    22	- D3: externally labeled, magnitude-restricted validation on real ZTF
    23	  photometry (detection completeness, frequency recovery, negative-class
    24	  trigger rate).
    25	Banned phrases (G1): "quantified selection-function measurement", "real-sky
    26	completeness" (for D2), "D3 FPR", unqualified "purity". Estimand names in
    27	METRICS_SPEC.md are binding.
    28	
    29	## Frozen-core / adapter-shell architecture
    30	
    31	- Tag `frozen-2026-08-01` = branch point. Zero edits to any script that
    32	  produced the published bundle; the referee check is an empty
    33	  `git diff frozen-2026-08-01 -- scripts/<frozen five>`.
    34	- Frozen five: `run_catalog_lomb_scargle.py`, `run_lomb_scargle.py`,
    35	  `lomb_scargle_common.py`, `build_catalog_panels.py`,
    36	  `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py`. SHA-256 pinned in
