   108	## D3 — ZTF × Kepler delta Scuti (real ZTF light curves, external labels)
   109	
   110	- Labels: Murphy+2019 (VizieR J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1, 14,330 Kepler A/F
   111	  stars; `dSct` flag 0/1/2 — ships its own labeled negative class).
   112	- Amplitude axis: Mo+2026 (J/A+A/710/A245): table2 = 259,883 extracted
   113	  frequencies (SNR>8) for 1,838 delta Scutis → per-star dominant amplitude
   114	  (ppt × 1.0857 → mmag); table1 = confirmed super-Nyquist modes → the
   115	  sub-hour stratum (any confirmed SNF ⇒ real mode above Kepler LC Nyquist
   116	  283.2 µHz ⇒ P < 59 min). This replaces the originally scouted Bowman+2016
   117	  join: Bowman's VizieR table carries no amplitudes; Mo+2026 supersedes it
   118	  (and is itself the published Murphy×Bowman merge, 1,838 stars).
   119	- Roster (`build_d3_roster.py`, rebuilt 2026-08-28 post-G1): gmag ≥ 13.2
   120	  (Murphy/KIC g magnitude — the named saturation proxy), ALL 610 dSct=1
   121	  survivors + ALL 76 dSct=2 (own class, excluded from headline numbers) +
   122	  2,314 dSct=0 negatives as a frozen-seed (20260828) simple random sample
   123	  (inclusion probability exactly 2314/7292, weight exactly 7292/2314;
   124	  sampling_weight column carried into every weighted estimate) = 3,000.
   125	  Before any campaign L-S run, the realized crossmatch mapping and an
   126	  ambiguity-adjudication file are committed (crossmatch frozen as DATA,
   127	  not just procedure). Amplitude coverage of positives:
   128	  456/610 with dominant amplitude; 48 > 10 mmag; 254 in 1–10; 154 < 1;
   129	  290 sub-hour; median 1.77 mmag. The 1–10 mmag log ladder and the
   130	  sub-threshold majority make the completeness turn-on curve the headline
   131	  D3 deliverable, not a defect (pre-registered: risk 2).
   132	  Sub-hour stratum caveat (binding): a confirmed Mo super-Nyquist frequency
   133	  establishes a sub-hour signal in the KEPLER APERTURE, not automatically
   134	  in the ZTF-matched source (blends), and the per-star dominant amplitude
   135	  need not describe the super-Nyquist mode; sub-hour-stratum detections are
   136	  adjudicated in W4 alongside triggered negatives, and Mo amplitude
   137	  sinc-correction status gets verified against the paper in W3.
