   151	## D2 — TESS-truth transplant (DAV signals in real ZTF windows)
   152	
   153	- Truth: Romero+2022 (MNRAS 511, 1574; arXiv:2201.04158; 74 new DAVs,
   154	  TESS Cy1–3) + Romero+2025 (ApJ 984, 112; arXiv:2407.07260; 32 new DAVs,
   155	  Cy4–5). Published per-mode tables: period [s] + amplitude [ppt] + per-star
   156	  FAP(1/1000) limit + 20-s-cadence flags. 2025 revisions apply: NOV
   157	  retractions (TIC 261400271, 804835539, 317620456) and updated mode lists
   158	  for re-observed 2022 objects — latest published solution wins.
   159	- Truth model, not interpolation (`d2_truth_model.py`): for 120-s sampling,
   160	  DAV P < 240 s is super-Nyquist (Nyquist period 240 s) and the boxcar
   161	  integration response has its first null at P = 120 s — two distinct
   162	  boundaries, both making interpolated TESS photometry undefined in the DAV
   163	  range; the mode table is evaluated analytically at the template's real
   164	  `bjd_tdb`. Chain: ppt → mag (×1.0857e-3) → crowding: the published
   165	  amplitudes are PDCSAP, already dilution-corrected (Romero+2022 §2,
   166	  Romero+2025 §2), so no de-dilution is applied; the prespecified crowding
   167	  SENSITIVITY is the SAP-equivalent RE-dilution A × CROWDSAP (multiplication;
   168	  Amendment 2 — the pre-G3 text's "divide by CROWDSAP" would have inflated
   169	  amplitudes ~5× at the median CROWDSAP 0.19), scheduled only for
   170	  SPOC-verified targets whose CROWDSAP is on file →
   171	  de-integrate the TESS boxcar (signed sinc; REJECT modes with
   172	  |sinc| < 0.3, i.e. P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence, P < ~27 s at 20-s);
   173	  cadence precedence is algorithmic: cadence_s (an EFFECTIVE integration
   174	  time; TESS timestamps are exposure midpoints, as the signed-sinc algebra
   175	  assumes) = 20 iff the star's chosen published solution includes any "f"
   176	  (20-s) sector, else 120 →
   177	  bandpass ladder A_g/A_TESS ∈ {1.4, 1.7, 2.1} × A_r/A_g ∈
   178	  {0.70, 0.80, 0.90} — a PHENOMENOLOGICAL SENSITIVITY GRID, not a derived
   179	  physical range: the blackbody T-derivative at 11,500 K gives (1.43, 0.80)
   180	  ≈ the low rung (not band-integrated, no limb darkening, l-independent);
   181	  the ADOPTED nominal (1.7, 0.80) is the grid midpoint; DA-atmosphere
   182	  band-integrated validation of the endpoints is a stated limitation (the
   183	  ladder is non-optional — zr carries most published confirmations) →
   184	  re-integrate the ZTF 30-s boxcar analytically → compose with the FROZEN
   185	  phase protocol: one independent phase per mode; base assignment
   186	  (phase_draw = 0) seeds PCG64(TIC) and is shared across bands and across
   187	  every bandpass/de-dilution/amplitude-scale variant; the two phase-draw
   188	  sensitivity variants d ∈ {1, 2} seed PCG64(TIC·10 + d) and change ONLY
   189	  the phase vector; shared t_ref keeps the frozen two-band rule meaningful.
   190	- Windows: templates from ALL 928 stars of the published catalog (G1 fix —
   191	  the earlier 510-not-detected pool conditioned on the pipeline's own
   192	  outcome), matched by median zg mag (|Δg| ≤ 0.25, widened when thin;
   193	  flagged), K=3 per target at the 10/50/90th-percentile positions of the
   194	  matched pool sorted by W_g (Amendment 4; W_g = Σ_nights max(n_zg,night − 1,
   195	  0) = the zg support that survives the frozen nightly-median subtraction —
   196	  the pre-pilot "median exposures-per-night" covariate is degenerate: pool
   197	  quantiles 1.0/1.0/2.0, K0 == K1 for 103/103 targets; W_g's pool 10/50/90th
   198	  percentiles are 6/58/452 and give strictly distinct K0 < K1 < K2 for every
   199	  target; 75% of zg nights are single-exposure; per-night median subtraction
   200	  annihilates 53% of zg data — pre-registered, stratified: risk 3).
   201	  Template matching is a TOTAL deterministic algorithm (zero analyst
   202	  discretion): candidate pool = stars with |median_zg − target_G| ≤ 0.25;
   203	  if fewer than 3, the pool widens once to ≤ 0.5; if still fewer than 3,
   204	  the pool is the 9 smallest |Δmag| stars, magnitude ties broken by
   205	  ascending source_id (pandas argsort is stable over the source_id-sorted
   206	  stats table); the pool is then sorted lexicographically by
   207	  (W_g, source_id) — a total order, so no residual ties — and picks are
   208	  indices round-half-even(q·(n−1)) for q ∈ {0.10, 0.50, 0.90} (numpy
   209	  round); W_g is recorded per shard and production refuses any target whose
   210	  three windows are not strictly increasing in W_g. Match label recorded per
   211	  target. D2 PRIMARY estimand (Amendment 4) is injected-signal RECOVERY:
   212	  rule 1 fires AND the best candidate directly matches the largest-amplitude
   213	  retained injected mode; post-injection rule firing (detection-only) is the
   214	  secondary "post-injection rule-1 trigger rate" — the pilot showed 45% of
   215	  matched windows are published variables on which detection-only mostly
   216	  measures native triggers (confirmed 11/13, recovered 2/13);
   217	  native variability in the pool is contextualized by PAIRED UNINJECTED
   218	  CONTROLS (95-prefix; stable ids indexed over the sorted 928 pool): one
   219	  control shard per unique arm-B template window. W2 stretch: fetch real
   220	  ZTF light curves at the 103 Romero positions; usable self-windows form a
   221	  SEPARATE DIAGNOSTIC arm — they do not replace or enter the nominal K=3
   222	  aggregate.
   223	- Arms: B primary (signal + real ZTF mags, real magerr), A diagnostic for
   224	  positive injections; arm-A ZERO-AMPLITUDE NULLS are the campaign's sole
   225	  confirmatory endpoint (P5, METRICS_SPEC). Gaussian-null false-alarm rate
   226	  (`FPR_Gaussian`): 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude simulations scheduled over
   227	  the 928-window frame by deterministic cycling (serial i → sorted-pool
   228	  window i mod 928, noise seed = serial); windows repeat, seeds do not.
   229	  Verification arm: ~20 SPOC light curves prewhitened to confirm published
   230	  solutions; everything else needs metadata only.
   231	- Run matrix (22 workers ≈ 84 runs/h). CORE scheduled total ≤ 3,299 ≈
   232	  1.6 d (3,266 + the 33 Amendment-3 `cadence_alt` shards), all binding: arm B nominal (1.7/0.80) 103×3 = 309; arm A nominal
   233	  309; Gaussian nulls 1,000; paired controls ≤ 309 (unique arm-B windows);
   234	  ladder sensitivity MEDIAN-WINDOW-CONDITIONED: 8 non-nominal (R_g, R_rg)
   235	  points × 103 × 1 = 824; phase-draw sensitivity 2 × 103 = 206;
   236	  amplitude-stationarity axis (scale × {0.7, 1.3}) 2 × 103 = 206;
   237	  dominant-mode-dropout variant ≤ 103 (targets with ≥ 2 RETAINED modes;
   238	  the dropped mode is the largest-amplitude retained mode; every survivor
   239	  keeps its nominal phase — Amendment 2) — the ±30% multiplier is a LOCAL
   240	  sensitivity, not an astrophysical envelope; DAV modes can vanish outright

