     1	# METRICS_SPEC — to be frozen at G2 (freeze = git blob SHA recorded in
     2	# GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md when the G2 panel reaches no-blocker verdicts)
     3	
     4	Implemented by `scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py`. Any change
     5	after the first campaign L-S run voids the prespecification and must be
     6	reported as such. v3, 2026-08-28: absorbs G2 round-2 findings (referee2,
     7	stats2, methods2, abstract lenses). v4, 2026-08-30 (Amendment 4): a DISCLOSED
     8	post-pilot, pre-confirmatory amendment — the gen1 timing pilot (non-
     9	confirmatory, archived, entering no estimate) exposed a degenerate D2 window
    10	stratification and a construct-validity defect in detection-only P4; both
    11	are repaired here BEFORE any confirmatory-era run, and no further hierarchy
    12	change is permitted after Amendment 4.
    13	
    14	## Estimand vocabulary (names are binding)
    15	
    16	Three separate response assessments; never pooled.
    17	
    18	- **detection completeness** — P(rule fires | labeled positive), reported for
    19	  BOTH denominators: `eligible_roster` (missing/unusable light curves count
    20	  as non-detections) and `usable_lightcurve` (frozen QC passed, both passes
    21	  complete). D1 denominators: the 13 paper-variable stars of the published
    22	  19-star master table (the 928-star catalog is NOT a labeled-positive
    23	  completeness denominator). D3: the 610 dSct=1 survivors. D2: injection
    24	  targets — always labeled *conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the
    25	  search stage*. Amendment 4: the D2 PRIMARY endpoint is injected-signal
    26	  RECOVERY (rule 1 fires AND the best candidate directly matches the
    27	  largest-amplitude retained injected mode, `endpoint = recovery`);
    28	  post-injection rule firing (detection-only) is the SECONDARY
    29	  "post-injection rule-1 trigger rate" (`endpoint = trigger`) and carries no
    30	  recovery or completeness interpretation; paired uninjected controls
    31	  contextualize native triggers and never enter the primary denominator.
    32	- **frequency-recovery completeness** — P(rule fires AND
    33	  best_candidate_matches_dominant | labeled positive AND freq-scorable AND
    34	  S_p = 1). Freq-scorable: D3 = Mo-joined with >=1 frequency and a defined
    35	  dominant amplitude (assert count == 456; "Mo-join-conditioned" label
    36	  mandatory; joined-vs-unjoined covariate table mandatory); D2 = >=1
    37	  RETAINED injected mode (from injected_modes.csv, post |sinc|>=0.3
    38	  rejection — never the original mode table); D1 = diagnostic only
    39	  (non-contemporaneous literature frequencies; see below).
    40	  S_p (per pass p): >=1 truth frequency inside pass p's search bounds
    41	  (low: [2/baseline, 48] / d; high: [24, 1440] / d); S_best = S_low OR
    42	  S_high. Known consequence stated up front: only ~10/456 D3 dominant
    43	  frequencies lie >= 24 / d, so D3 high-pass frequency recovery is a
    44	  near-empty cell and is reported as counts.
    45	  Mo-join MNAR limitation (binding statement): Mo inclusion required
    46	  SNR > 8 in Kepler photometry and is plausibly related to amplitude,
    47	  magnitude, and mode complexity; missingness for the 154 unjoined
    48	  positives is treated as informative — the frequency-recovery curve is
    49	  therefore a Mo-join-conditioned estimand, the joined-vs-unjoined
    50	  covariate table is mandatory, and DETECTION surfaces retain all 610
    51	  positives with the unjoined stars in an explicit `amp_unknown` bin so
    52	  their detection behavior is visible beside the joined sample.
    53	  The missed-vs-wrong-frequency decomposition uses matching denominators
    54	  only: P(D AND M | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1) vs P(D | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    55	- **correct-frequency fraction among detected positives** —
    56	  P(best_candidate_matches_dominant | rule-1 fired, Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    57	  Never called purity.
    58	- **frame-specific label PPV (D3 only)** — among triggered roster members of
    59	  the weighted frame {dSct=1 census positives, dSct=0 SRS negatives; dSct=2
    60	  EXCLUDED, reported separately}: weighted fraction labeled dSct=1.
    61	  Interval: FPC-rescaled survey bootstrap (B=2000, frozen seed): the 2,314
    62	  negatives are resampled with replacement, positives held fixed (census),
    63	  and bootstrap deviations are rescaled by sqrt(1 − f) with sampling
    64	  fraction f = 2314/7292 (SRSWOR finite-population correction).
    65	  No transfer to other prevalences. Output: ppv.csv.
    66	- **negative-class trigger rate (D3)** — P(rule fires | dSct=0, the
    67	  NON-dSct COMPARISON CLASS — it contains genuine gamma Dor, rotational,
    68	  binary and other variables, which is why this is a trigger rate). Weights are
    69	  constant within the class and cancel: plain Wilson on the 2,314 sampled
    70	  negatives (no FPC — conservative). Triggered negatives adjudicated in W4
    71	  (plausible real variable vs unexplained), reported descriptively.
    72	- **Gaussian-null false-alarm rate (FPR_Gaussian, D2)** — P(confirmed |
    73	  arm-A zero-amplitude null), n = 1000; window allocation frozen as
    74	  deterministic cycling of the sorted 928-window pool (serial i -> window
    75	  i mod 928), noise seed = serial. Interval: EXACT one-sided
    76	  Clopper-Pearson upper bound at the OBSERVED event count x
    77	  (U = Beta_{0.95}(x+1, n-x)); acceptance criterion (confirmatory):
    78	  U_95(x, 1000) <= 0.005. Windows repeat; inference is conditional on the
    79	  frozen window set. FP frequency-distribution/alias audit descriptive only
    80	  below 10 events.
    81	- **native trigger rate of the template pool (D2)** — P(confirmed | paired
    82	  uninjected control window, 95-prefix). Context, not an FPR.
    83	
    84	Exact D3 sampling constants (binding): negatives inclusion probability
    85	2314/7292 (= 0.31733406...), sampling weight 7292/2314 (= 3.15125324...);
    86	never derived from rounded values.
    87	
    88	## D1 specifics
    89	
    90	Labels from the published master table (19 usable stars: 13 paper-variable,
    91	5 paper-constant, 1 transit control excluded from both classes — it is the
    92	frozen pipeline's eclipsing sanity object). D1 truth frequencies are
    93	non-contemporaneous single-epoch literature tabulations of multi-mode
    94	pulsators (observed lit-vs-ZTF offsets reach 0.6%): frequency-recovery for
    95	D1 is DIAGNOSTIC only; the D1 estimand is detection completeness.
    96	Match tolerance adds a truth-quantum term: D1 +0.0025 / d (2-decimal
    97	tables); D2/D3 +0. Validation on record (2026-08-28): the engine reproduces
    98	all five published D1 numbers (11/13 L-S, 9/13 census, 13/13 union,
    99	0 confirmed + 1 candidate among the 5 constants).
   100	
   101	## Frequency-match taxonomy (evaluate everything, then classify)
   102	
   103	Tolerance: 1.5 / baseline_days + truth-quantum. f_sid = 1.00273790935 / d
   104	(frozen, the pipeline's constant). For each detected candidate, evaluate ALL
   105	(truth mode, relation) hits across the star's full truth list:
   106	  direct       |f_cand - f_t| <= tol
   107	  harmonic     |f_cand - 2 f_t| <= tol or |f_cand - f_t/2| <= tol
   108	  window_alias |f_cand - |f_t +/- k f_sid|| <= tol, k = 1, 2
   109	Classification: no hits -> `unmatched`; hits in exactly one relation class ->
   110	that class (several DIRECT hits on different modes remain `direct`); hits in
   111	more than one relation class -> `ambiguous` (excluded from strict recovery).
   112	Named estimator columns encode both axes:
   113	`best_candidate_matches_dominant` (headline; D3 dominant Mo mode / D2
   114	largest-amplitude retained injected mode; D1 diagnostic) and
   115	`best_candidate_matches_any_mode` (secondary), plus
   116	`any_top_peak_matches_any_mode` (diagnostic over the 15 stored peaks).
   117	Chance-match calibration: truth lists permuted across stars (frozen seed
   118	20260829, 100 permutations) -> accidental direct-match rate beside every
   119	frequency-recovery table.
   120	
   121	## Detection rules and the preregistered primary family
   122	
   123	Rules (all four always reported): 1 `confirmed`, 2 `confirmed|candidate`,
   124	3 `census` (any of six frozen ratios >= 2.5), 4 `either` (1 OR 3).
   125	PRIMARY endpoints — complete tuples; everything else is pointwise
   126	descriptive sensitivity:
   127	  P1 D3 detection completeness: {D3, dSct=1 (610), eligible_roster, rule 1,
   128	     best pass, unweighted, Wilson 95%}.
   129	  P2 D3 frequency recovery: {D3, Mo-joined S_best=1 subset, usable, rule 1 +
   130	     best_candidate_matches_dominant, Wilson 95%, beside chance-match rate}.
   131	  P3 D3 negative-class trigger rate: {D3, dSct=0 (2314), rule 1, best pass,
   132	     plain Wilson}.
   133	  P4 D2 conditional injection-recovery, algebraically (Amendment 4):
   134	     p-hat = (1/103) Σ_t (1/|K_t|) Σ_{k in K_t} y_{t,k}, where y_{t,k} = 1
   135	     iff rule 1 fires AND best_candidate_matches_dominant == direct (the
   136	     largest-amplitude RETAINED injected mode from injected_modes.csv) on
   137	     target t's stratum-k nominal (1.7/0.80, PDCSAP as published,
   138	     phase_draw 0, cadence rule) arm-B shard, and K_t ⊆
   139	     {0, 1, 2} is the set of strata with a usable result. ELIGIBLE variant:
   140	     denominator all 103 targets; missing stratum counts y = 0 with
   141	     |K_t| = n_strata_scheduled (3 for the nominal scenario; 1 for the
   142	     single-window sensitivity scenarios — Amendment 2); a K_t = ∅ target
   143	     contributes 0. USABLE variant:
   144	     p-hat_u = (1/(103 − n_∅)) Σ_{t: K_t ≠ ∅} (1/|K_t|) Σ_k y_{t,k} —
   145	     K_t = ∅ targets are excluded from numerator AND denominator, with
   146	     n_∅ reported as n_targets_zero_usable_strata. The bootstrap resamples
   147	     all 103 target labels with the common draw matrix for both variants;
   148	     a resampled-in K_t = ∅ target contributes 0 to the eligible statistic
   149	     and is dropped from that replicate's usable statistic (matching the
   150	     estimators). Both variants reported. Interval: target-cluster
   151	     bootstrap 95%.
   152	  P5 FPR_Gaussian acceptance: {D2 arm A nulls, rule 1, exact one-sided CP
   153	     upper at observed x <= 0.5%} — the sole confirmatory decision.
   154	No claim direction reversal, endpoint swap, or denominator swap after the
   155	first campaign L-S run. Flags: `prespecified_primary` marks the P4 recovery
   156	rows (nominal arm B, non-pilot) and the P5 row; `confirmatory_decision` is
   157	True only on the P5 row when its acceptance rule passes (P5 is the SOLE
   158	confirmatory decision). Paired controls (Amendment 4): every nominal arm-B
   159	shard is scored against its paired uninjected control for detection D and
   160	strict recovery R (the control's candidate frequency matched against the
   161	B target's dominant injected mode); report the 2×2 counts, B-only/C-only/
   162	union yields, target-standardized paired differences and P(R_B=1, R_C=0)
   163	with the common target-cluster draws, the quiet-control-conditioned
   164	secondary estimand (pairs whose control is usable and not_detected; report
   165	|T_Q|, pairs, unique windows), and the control reuse table. No aggregate
   166	native-rate subtraction; no conditioning of the primary denominator.
   167	
   168	## Units of analysis and intervals
   169	
   170	- D1/D3: the star is the unit. Wilson 95% on unweighted proportions; plain
   171	  Wilson on the negatives class (weights cancel); survey bootstrap for PPV;
